# {{project_name}}

A token faucet dispensing a fixed amount per address with a cooldown,
generated by [soroban-forge](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge)
from the `faucet` template.

## How it works

1. **Fund** — the admin deposits tokens into the faucet.
2. **Claim** — any address calls `claim` to receive a fixed
   `amount_per_claim` of the configured token.
3. **Cooldown** — an address must wait `cooldown_seconds` between
   successive claims; claiming early reverts.

## Develop

```sh
cargo test                 # run unit tests
stellar contract build     # build the deployable wasm
```

## Deploy to testnet

```sh
stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/wasm32v1-none/release/{{crate_name}}.wasm \
  --source-account <your-identity> \
  --network testnet
```

Then initialize and fund:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <ADMIN> \
  --network testnet \
  -- initialize \
  --admin <ADMIN_ADDRESS> \
  --token <TOKEN_ADDRESS> \
  --amount_per_claim 100 \
  --cooldown_seconds 86400

stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <ADMIN> \
  --network testnet \
  -- fund \
  --amount 1000000
```

Claim tokens:

```sh
stellar contract invoke \
  --id <CONTRACT_ID> \
  --source-account <CLAIMANT> \
  --network testnet \
  -- claim \
  --to <CLAIMANT_ADDRESS>
```

## Security

This template is a starting point, not audited code. See [security-considerations.md](https://github.com/soroban-forge-labs/soroban-forge/blob/main/docs/security-considerations.md) for what it does and does not protect against.
